Measure control quality as well as processing time
Faster approval can reduce administrative delay, but it does not demonstrate safer work on its own. Consider measures that reveal whether the process is functioning:

Permits returned because the scope or evidence was incomplete.
Changes requiring reassessment that received the necessary review.
Handover records with acknowledged responsibility.
Repeated permit exceptions by activity or location.
Closure records awaiting required verification.
AI suggestions accepted, rejected or corrected after review.
Define each measure clearly. A rise in permits returned for correction may initially reflect more effective scrutiny rather than worsening preparation. Review the underlying cases before drawing conclusions.

Start with a controlled pilot
Choose a representative activity and involve the people who request, review, issue and receive permits. Test ordinary work alongside difficult cases: changed scope, overlapping activity, an unavailable approver, interrupted connectivity and unfinished work at shift change.

For AI-assisted functions, inspect the evidence behind suggestions and record missed issues as well as unnecessary alerts. Agree access permissions, audit records and fallback arrangements before expanding the rollout.

The aim is a process the team can understand and use reliably under operational pressure.

Frequently asked questions
What is the difference between digital PTW and AI-powered PTW?
Digital PTW manages forms, approvals, status and records electronically. AI-assisted PTW adds analysis that may help interpret task information and identify patterns or inconsistencies. Fixed workflow rules remain important in both.

Can AI approve a high-risk work permit?
AI recommendations should not replace the authorised person’s decision or required field checks. Approval must follow the organisation’s defined responsibilities and procedures.

Can one permit cover several interacting jobs?
That depends on the site’s permit rules and how the work is defined. Interdependent activities require explicit coordination; combining records for convenience must not obscure ownership or controls.

Does software guarantee compliance?
No. Software can support documentation and workflow consistency. Compliance depends on applicable requirements, competent people and how work is actually controlled.

